  "description": "T1 Magnolia (Magnolia sp.) - Sensitive crown prune and reshapeCarry out a light, selective crown prune to improve form and manage canopy size while retaining the tree's natural habit. Works to include:Remove dead, damaged, diseased and crossing branches throughout the crown.Lightly reduce and reshape outer crown where required, targeting a balanced outline and improved clearance from surrounding features.Reductions to be taken back to suitable secondary growth/branch junctions, avoiding heading cuts and minimising wound size.Maintain an even distribution of crown density and flowering framework; no excessive thinning or over reduction.&nbsp;&nbsp;Reduce by 0.75 – 1m circaT2 Bay (Laurus nobilis) - Crown reshapeReshape the crown to form a neat, balanced canopy appropriate to its setting. Works to include:Selective tip pruning and minor reductions to restore symmetry and contain spread.Cuts to suitable growth points to encourage dense, healthy regrowth and maintain a natural outline.Retain sufficient live foliage to support vigour; avoid creating voids or harsh edges.&nbsp;&nbsp;Reduce height by 1m and reshapeReason for works:Regular tree maintenance",
